SUMMARY:Bear Pen Gap\; a Saunter.
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We wi
 ll get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike
  groups don’t !!\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY**\nI am 
 going to try to find the blueberry field of the Bear Pen Gap section of th
 e MST. A few ppl are welcome to join me.\nHike Distance: 3.0 mi (apprx) Ac
 cum ascent: 500 ft.\nElevation: 5\,500 ft\nPace: **1.5mph – because I’
 m an ol’ Codger.**\nDifficulty: Very Rocky w/ roots. Single track\; In &
  Out.\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive time: 35mi/1 hr 1-w
 ay\nReturn Not earlier than: : 2:30 pm **(=4.5 hrs)**\nCarpool contributio
 ns appreciated. $5.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Waynesville\, NC\n*https:/
 /www.mountain-forecast.com/peaks/Richland-Balsam/forecasts/1954*\nWeather 
 cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED A
 S DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 2.0 driver(s). (=9ppl)\nWe suggest op
 en windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge
  accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.
 \nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes i
 nto the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers will be 
 assumed to be having an affair. Obstreperous raucous yawping is discourage
 d. My attempts to quiet the prattlers has failed. This has become a ‘soc
 ial networking’ event.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event i
 s NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. 
 Well trained dogs **(you don’t have to yell)** can be 'off-leash'. 'On l
 eash' while meeting others on the trail.. Small (lap)dogs may carpool. Lar
 ge dogs will drive themselves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by
  ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\nWood elves are 
 mischievous in the Summer\; Zip your backpacks tight.\nAll hikes are at yo
 ur own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipmen
 t.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a profess
 ional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this event.
  There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participan
 t\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability 
 the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and member
 s for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur
  while participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle du
 ring this trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules an
 d regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\
 , and not to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s
 ) also has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recordin
 g on website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.c
 om\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https://
 www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
